    "context": "## What I found\n- The workspace is empty \u2014 no existing files to worry about.\n\n## Why this plan\n- The starter CSS sets `--fg: #ffffff` and `--bg: #ffffff`, meaning white text on a white background \u2014 the text will be invisible. After serving, I'll need to adjust the colors (likely making the background dark or the text dark) so the page is actually readable. The plan accounts for this in step 3.\n- The HTML will be straightforward: an `h1` with \"Build Status: GREEN\" and a short `<p>`.\n\n## Trade-offs\n- I'll keep the starter sheet structure intact (variables, selectors) and only change the color values if the preview confirms the visibility issue. This respects the instruction to keep it as-is unless the running page shows a problem."
